' The intro (`IntroScene`) as the program starts, then skipped with a click
' (`IntroScene.cs:135-139`). Run with `menu snaps <dir>`; add
' `menushot <dir>/menu.png` (and leave out headless.sh's `do quit`) to see
' the start screen it leads to. A scripted run's intro clock is 16 ms a
' frame, so the times below are frames x 16 ms: page 1 begins at 6.1 s,
' page 2 at 15.2, 3 at 22.3, 4 at 36.4, 5 at 41.6, 6 at 54.7.
wait 186
snap intro_03s_page0      ' map 89
wait 437
snap intro_10s_ani0       ' map 81, intro1.ani 0-2
wait 498
snap intro_18s_page2      ' map 80, scrolled left 30 px a second
wait 467
snap intro_25s_ani4       ' map 82, intro2.ani 0-2
wait 779
snap intro_38s_page4      ' map 90, in map 0's colours
wait 467
snap intro_45s_ani6       ' map 83 scrolling, intro3.ani 0-2
wait 935
snap intro_60s_ani10      ' map 84, intro4.ani 0-2
menuclick 160,100         ' any click: the start screen
